  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNESCO Sexality Education in Schools</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO Sexuality Education in School Programme - UNECO Sexuality Education in School Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Main Objective: Increased access to high quality &amp; age appropriate sexuality education &amp; services for young people (aged 10 &#x2013; 24).
Sub-Objectives
1. Strengthen the quality, delivery and effectiveness of comprehensive sexuality education (CSE) curricula to ensure that they are evidence based-gender transformative, and age-and culturally appropriate.2. Ensure access to quality and age appropriate sexual reproductive health information and health services for adolescents and young people (aged 10 &#x2013; 24) including young people living with HIV (YPLHIV) and those with disabilities in supported project sites.3. Strengthen Zambia&#x2019;s ability to protect children against sexual violence &amp; harassment in school settings4. Improve community engagement in young people&#x2019;s access to comprehensive sexuality education &amp; services5. Improve research and evaluation around SRH for young people aged 10 &#x2013; 24 years to enhance the evidence base for planning and implementation of programmes</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet syftar till att inf&#xf6;ra omfattande sexuell upplysning i skolor i Zambia f&#xf6;r att leverera tillr&#xe4;cklig kunskap och information och g&#xf6;ra det m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r ungdomar att fatta v&#xe4;lgrundade beslut om sin sexualitet och sexuell h&#xe4;lsa. Det slutliga m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra den sexuella och reproduktiva h&#xe4;lsa, minska oplanerade pregnacies och slutligen l&#xe4;gre avhopp fr&#xe5;n skolan.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at introducing Comprehensive  Sexuality Education in schools in Zambia in order to deliver appropriate knowledge and information and enable adolescents  to make informed choices about their sexuality and sexual health. The ultimate goal is to improve sexual and reproductive Health, reduce unplanned pregnacies and ultimately lower  school dropouts.</narrative>
  </description>
